ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"aab1e64e4ccf1bee85f5af94155000ff74462a08efb4f5276103abe0691c030f","event_uuid":"605c4222-897a-4c71-aac9-35fd5ce999d7","position":{"commit_sha":"bad1c749b0648f0d25d38372f4dbec4feadb2955","position":"1786995474946605001-605c4222-897a-4c71-aac9-35fd5ce999d7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"801dd612ed9b8e654439fc223a39edbea186faa1a0d2a29c7b6d50e7c63161d3","event_uuid":"14f57ade-a49a-48c8-9053-eef9a870f29d","position":{"commit_sha":"eb3ef2725755256eb347ff9ba7973abdbdf9b6d1","position":"1786995501125680001-14f57ade-a49a-48c8-9053-eef9a870f29d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"234695c4965d820df64628dfe8292ee7465a4183b3e57dea24a30ac1886b27d1","event_uuid":"738eeaf7-2e41-4008-9b7e-d1ea459ab78c","position":{"commit_sha":"3ea983354d7577c2dff6308e8f0f5887f90e5714","position":"1786995583523155001-738eeaf7-2e41-4008-9b7e-d1ea459ab78c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"492487cdf607f49e5ed277388109697944cdbd5a8d31515123bcc55dcabf0d01","event_uuid":"12c74955-2a02-4fb5-b75d-a3f394e147f4","position":{"commit_sha":"c90022019042d1697ec1708af8f2bf3f8f0ebb2d","position":"1786995725826217001-12c74955-2a02-4fb5-b75d-a3f394e147f4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786995161367646001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a28cf847-53a9-42eb-96f2-750e2e7787e1","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe S1 snapshot exists in shadow mode, but reconciler read/check paths still call `load_config()`, inspect environment/cwd, hard-code tracker layout, and build Jira backends whose properties can reload ambient settings. This can change read scope during one run or discard the supplied registry config.\n\n## Outcome\nCut `reconcile-check` and dry-run fetch/diff/preflight paths over to focused immutable `ReconcilerSettings`, `GitRuntime`, and selected `BridgeRuntime` projections. Construct exactly one selected Jira Cloud or Jira Data Center backend from those bindings; its project/query scope, TLS, timeout/limits, tracker layout, and auth capability remain stable for the operation.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py` for the focused reconciler/Git/bridge projection and provider-specific Jira static-auth carriers, composed from the S1 snapshot seam. Static fields use non-serializable Pydantic `SecretStr`/`SecretBytes`, are excluded from repr/equality/hash/cache/fingerprint, and unwrap only in the selected Jira sending adapter.\n2. Change `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_backend_registry.py` and Jira Cloud/DC factories/settings to consume the supplied projection/binding. Do not construct the unselected backend. Preserve official Jira client/ACLI TLS, timeout, retry, error, and close behavior.\n3. Thread the same backend/runtime through preflight, access check, fetch, paging, inbound/outbound diff, mapper/sanitizer/property access, tracker/binding reads, and Git ref/layout owners. Remove ambient reloads from those read/check call paths.\n4. Apply approved deltas explicitly: supplied Python config remains authoritative; custom tracker directory/branch/remote reaches every read owner; empty Cloud read scope fails closed; malformed config/auth fails before provider request. No write/apply path is cut over here.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Component tests construct a backend, monkeypatch every ambient resolver to raise, then exercise project/query properties, access check, paged fetch, inbound/outbound diff, mapper, sanitizer, binding lookup, and custom tracker ref reads.\n- Interface tests run Cloud and DC `reconcile-check`/dry-run through CLI, Python, MCP, and direct-module paths against verified fake transports. The oracle is provider request parameters plus provider-neutral result, not private implementation shape.\n- Failure tests use missing/conflicting auth, empty project/query scope, malformed TLS/URL/config, and the unselected provider's poison constructor; assert zero Jira model request/local write and typed/redacted errors.\n- Secret canaries cover carriers, backend repr, exceptions, logs, provenance, request URL/query, cache/fingerprint, and the unselected adapter.\n- Existing Jira auth/TLS/retry/output fixtures and ticket-sourced regressions are a required baseline; any deliberate difference is named in the ticket comment before implementation changes it.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nKeep a read-only compatibility facade that can delegate the read/check call to legacy composition while S2 parity/deltas are measured. No stored format changes. Rollback selects that facade before S3 write cutover; secrets are never logged for comparison.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Cloud and DC read/check interface tests complete with all ambient resolvers poisoned after composition, proving one backend/settings authority for the operation.\n- [ ] Supplied config and custom tracker directory/branch/remote determine every observed read/ref/query owner; ambient root-B mutations cannot alter a root-A operation.\n- [ ] Backend project/query/TLS/timeout/limit properties remain unchanged after environment/file mutation and the next operation observes the new composition.\n- [ ] Exactly the selected Jira integration is constructed; missing/conflicting auth or decision-bearing scope fails before a Jira model request or local write with no anonymous/cross-provider/principal fallback.\n- [ ] Secret canaries are absent from every named carrier/backend/diagnostic/wire boundary, while the selected sending adapter can authenticate the verified fake request.\n- [ ] Existing read/check provider-neutral outputs stay equal except the approved explicit-input, fail-fast, and stable-property deltas; disabling the read facade restores legacy behavior.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py","reason":"New focused ReconcilerSettings, GitRuntime, BridgeRuntime, and static Jira carrier projections."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_backend_registry.py","reason":"Construct one selected backend from supplied operation bindings."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/","reason":"Cloud read/check settings, auth boundary, transport, mapper, and stable properties."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/","reason":"Data Center read/check settings, auth boundary, transport, and stable properties."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"Use injected backend/runtime for fetch and query scope."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py","reason":"Use injected backend mapper without ambient reload."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_preflight.py","reason":"Fail decision-bearing config/auth before provider request."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py","reason":"Use the selected stable backend/auth binding."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/","reason":"Cloud/DC stable-property, poisoned-ambient, failure, and secret-carrier oracles."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py","reason":"Provider-neutral read/check interface coverage across surfaces."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","a377-7fcd-4af0-4d11"],["parent","e215-ab23-ed6a-4791"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"e215-ab23-ed6a-4791","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp04","config","reconciler","jira"],"ticket_id":"e042-4780-6c63-4b09","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-04 S2 — Cut reconciler read/check paths to operation runtimes","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_operation_bindings.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Stable selected backend/runtime, poisoned ambient, failure, and secret carrier behavior"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC6","dd_text":"Provider-neutral read/check behavior through supported surfaces"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_config_validation.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_dc_config_settings.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_config_jira_wiring.py","dd_id":"REGRESSION","dd_text":"Existing Cloud/DC configuration, TLS, and settings lessons"}]},"source_event_uuids":["ccf589ef-fb2f-4eba-9182-b830f43519d7","b75ac9f0-fa88-4f11-8d1a-4200ea13c78b","a28cf847-53a9-42eb-96f2-750e2e7787e1","605c4222-897a-4c71-aac9-35fd5ce999d7","14f57ade-a49a-48c8-9053-eef9a870f29d","738eeaf7-2e41-4008-9b7e-d1ea459ab78c","12c74955-2a02-4fb5-b75d-a3f394e147f4"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786999215053041001,"uuid":"48446408-ed7b-42d7-8922-8ff161dfd7e1"}